"Spell Books": {
  "index": -92,
  "category": "sorcery",
  "sections": [
    {
      "type": "title",
      "value": "Spell Books"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "json": [
        {
          "text": "Once I start gaining several spells, I'll need a place to carry them all. The spell book spells can be switched between simply by turning the pages, "
        },
        {
          "text": "assuming I've placed the spells on Vellum",
          "color": "dark_purple"
        },
        {
          "text": ". "
        },
        {
          "text": "(Hold Z and select from the wheel).",
          "italic": true
        },
        {
          "text": "\n\nSpells placed on "
        },
        {
          "text": "Staves, Wands, and Bangles",
          "color": "blue"
        },
        {
          "text": " cannot be placed into spell books, but those items instead can be "
        },
        {
          "text": "enchanted",
          "color": "blue"
        },
        {
          "text": "."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "title",
      "value": "Grimoires"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "json": [
        {
          "text": "I've seen wizards use a "
        },
        {
          "text": "Cantrip",
          "color": "blue"
        },
        {
          "text": " to summon books that they keep their spells in, once they have a little more experience with magic.  They referred to them as "
        },
        {
          "text": "Grimoires",
          "color": "blue"
        },
        {
          "text": ".\n\nI asked a wizard once why not just use a spell book, and they told me that while a Grimoire has less space than a Spell Book, it's "
        },
        {
          "text": "extradimensional",
          "color": "dark_purple"
        },
        {
          "text": ".  This means that "
        },
        {
          "text": "if the Grimoire is ever lost or destroyed, all they need to do is summon it back with another cantrip and it's back, contents and all",
          "color": "dark_purple"
        },
        {
          "text": ".  \nThe downside is that multiple Grimoires share the same extradimensional space, so having more than one doesn't grant much benefit.\n\nStill, sounds pretty useful.  Reminds me of an Ender Chest."
        },
        {
          "text": "\n\nSpell Books and Grimoires allow you to change the slot quickly using Chords.  Press the chord key (default V) with a Spell Book or Grimoire equipped, then press a hotbar key.  It will quick swap to the slot matching what you pressed.  This is in addition to the radial menu.  Use whatever method you prefer.",
          "italic": true
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "json": [
        {
          "text": "Both "
        },
        {
          "text": "Spell Books and Grimoires can be dyed",
          "color": "dark_purple"
        },
        {
          "text": " simply by crafting them together with dye. Be sure to "
        },
        {
          "text": "remove spells from them before doing so",
          "color": "dark_purple"
        },
        {
          "text": " as it's possible the crafting process can damage the spells within."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "json": [
        {
          "text": "I've even seen wizards that are aligned with a faction summon special grimoires that represent their faction!  They don't do anything different than a regular Grimoire, but they sure look flashy."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
